WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:05.460
Yennefer of Vengerberg comes from nothing, but&nbsp;
her determination and strength make her one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.660
of the most powerful and dangerous mages&nbsp;
in "The Witcher." On the Netflix series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:15.600
Yennefer is played by Anya Chalotra, and like&nbsp;
Yennefer in the books, Chalotra has long black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.060
hair. She wears violet contact lenses to&nbsp;
show her elven heritage. The show's Yen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.040
also often wears black and white clothing, the&nbsp;
character's preferred color scheme in the novels.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:31.260
In "The Witcher" video games, Yennefer is&nbsp;
voiced by Denise Gough and is introduced in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.780
"The Witcher 3: The Wild Hunt." The game version&nbsp;
of Yennefer is a closer match to the character in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.400
the books. Her hair is still black, but it&nbsp;
falls over her shoulders in a mass of dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.500
curls. She also has violet-colored eyes and&nbsp;
wears her trademark black and white attire.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.520
The video game Yennefer appears to&nbsp;
be some years older than Chalotra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.940
yet age doesn't mean much when&nbsp;
you are practically immortal.

